# options and -- after the first operand are operands (PCTS cp 97: "cp file1 file2 -p" copies into the
# directory ./-p, "cp file1 file2 --" into the directory ./--). posixutils-rs takes them as options.
a x -p
a --
# -H and -L are listed in the synopsis only with -R, but nothing in the spec makes them an error without it
# (a link is followed anyway). posixutils-rs insists on -R.
-H la x
-L la x
a -- 
